BREACHWATCH

Status: 🟠 Confirmed breach / published data / technical scope reconciliation continuing

What is confirmed

ADT experienced a cybersecurity incident involving unauthorized access.

ADT said certain cloud-based environments containing customer and prospective-customer information were affected.

ADT confirmed the exposed information primarily included:

Names
Telephone numbers
Physical addresses

ADT confirmed that a smaller percentage of records also contained:

Dates of birth
Last four digits of Social Security numbers
Last four digits of Tax IDs

ADT stated that payment information was not accessed.

ADT stated that customer security systems were not affected or compromised.

A dataset attributed to the ADT incident was subsequently published.

HIBP indexed approximately 5.5 million unique email addresses associated with the breach dataset.

What is claimed / reported

ShinyHunters carried out the attack.

Voice phishing / social engineering was used as the initial compromise mechanism.

An ADT employee or corporate identity was compromised.

The compromised identity provided access to ADT's cloud environment.

The attacker used legitimate or compromised authorization to reach customer data.

The incident involved extortion.

The precise identity, authentication and cloud-access sequence has not been publicly established by ADT.

